Chapter: StringBuilderAliasLocal
  cites Foreword chapter StringBuilder

 The other half of stringbuilder-alias, closing the gap its prose
 records: here the builder is a LOCAL bound from a call
 rather than a declared parameter. sb-new's registered return type is
 the mutable StringBuilder, so the binding owns the record the moment
 the call answers, and handing it to two owners is the same aliasing
 whichever way it arrived. Before the minted-mutable walk this chapter
 compiled clean and the in-place appends corrupted both results into
 alphabeta|alphabeta; the identical body with base as a parameter was
 already refused. Both shapes must be CDX2062.

 We say:

Section: Probe

  sbal-two-owners : Integer -> Text
  sbal-two-owners (x) =
    let base = sb-new
    in let a = sb-append base "alpha"
    in let b = sb-append base "beta"
    in sb-to-text a & "|" & sb-to-text b

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni (sbal-two-owners 0)
  end
